{"chunk_id": "8192236a9d6a", "text": "Krishna (Vasudeva) reveals Karna\u2019s true birth and urges him to join the Pandavas. Citing scriptural law, he argues that Karna\u2014born to Kunti before her marriage\u2014should rightfully be counted as Pandu\u2019s son and therefore the eldest Pandava and rightful king. Krishna paints a grand vision: the Pandavas, Draupadi, and many kingdoms honoring Karna as emperor while his brothers serve him. Karna responds with calm gratitude but refuses. He acknowledges the truth of his birth yet insists that loyalty binds him to the Suta parents who raised him and to Duryodhana, who trusted and elevated him. Betraying them would violate his sense of duty and honor. Karna even asks Krishna to keep the secret, fearing Yudhishthira would renounce the throne if he knew. The passage highlights Karna\u2019s tragic nobility\u2014choosing loyalty and fate over power and reconciliation.\nKrishna urges Karna to join the Pandavas as Kunti\u2019s eldest son and king, but Karna refuses out of loyalty to his foster parents and Duryodhana.\nThemes: loyalty vs birthright, identity and parentage, dharma and gratitude, prelude to Kurukshetra, moral conflict", "vector": [0.019660308957099915, -0.028188150376081467, -0.003913552034646273, -0.008025425486266613, -0.013578438200056553, 0.02323010377585888, -0.011886091902852058, -0.0017386218532919884, -0.05404932424426079, -0.010378845036029816, 0.017148232087492943, 0.010081362910568714, 0.01427917554974556, 0.010418510064482689, -0.022714465856552124, -0.0003218599013052881, 0.04299618676304817, -0.023758962750434875, 0.04003457725048065, -0.011039918288588524, 0.0020989065524190664, -0.018523264676332474, -0.004792778752744198, 0.006164505146443844, -0.02358708344399929, 0.024777013808488846, 0.0092417998239398, -0.025715738534927368, 0.02605949528515339, -0.029325196519494057, -0.014451054856181145, 0.01410729717463255, -0.008098144084215164, -0.006693363655358553, -0.030435798689723015, 0.0046407319